WEBVTT

NOTE
Narration over progressive instrumental music.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.974
Start in Simple Costing. Load a Sri Lanka Tour Library itinerary, then check dates, travellers, rooming and nationality.

2
00:00:12.974 --> 00:00:24.834
Review each day, with routes, hotels, meal plans, mileage and entrances together. Load matching rates for the selected trip.

3
00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:38.180
Review exchange rates, markup and sharing options. Missing rates remain clearly flagged; finish those checks before creating a quotation.

4
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:53.662
In Quotation Studio, review itinerary, hotels, services, prices and terms. Choose the appropriate guest or agent document format.

5
00:00:53.662 --> 00:01:05.894
The studio provides Word, PDF, preview and delivery controls. Review the final document before approval or customer release.

6
00:01:05.894 --> 00:01:18.496
The reservation workspace brings service costs and selling details together. Review the saved booking and its operational requirements.

7
00:01:18.496 --> 00:01:29.938
Use the voucher and email area to prepare service documents. Check supplier arrangements and recipients before anything is sent.

8
00:01:29.938 --> 00:01:42.773
Open Accounts from the reservation. Work through customer invoicing, supplier purchases, receipts and payments, then the cost centre.

9
00:01:42.773 --> 00:01:54.680
Review the customer invoice and its posting status. Financial values and identifiers are hidden in this promotional walkthrough.

10
00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:05.843
Review supplier purchases within the same booking. Check the document and approval state before posting any financial entry.

11
00:02:05.843 --> 00:02:17.006
Review receipt allocations and supplier payment checks. Recorded evidence and posted ledger balances remain distinct.

12
00:02:17.006 --> 00:02:28.123
Review the cost centre and posted ledger. Resolve open reconciliation checks before treating the booking accounts as final.